.nh
.TH "AXILIO" "1" "2026-08-02" "axilio 0.6.1" "Axilio CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
axilio \- Acquire and drive Axilio phones from the command line


.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
axilio [global options] <command> [command options]
.EE


.SH DESCRIPTION
Acquire Axilio phones, drive live sessions, run workflows, and manage
the resources that support them.

.PP
Start with login, acquire a session, observe its phone, then act on what
is visible. Sessions remain active in Axilio until stopped. The CLI also
saves session information locally so later phone commands can reconnect.

.PP
The main command families are:

.EX
phones / sessions   discover phones and manage active phone sessions
phone               observe and control the selected session's phone
workflows / runs    discover workflows and create or inspect runs
uploads             store media and deliver it to phones
api-keys            manage organization-scoped API keys
.EE

.PP
For detailed offline documentation, run man axilio. Run axilio help
--html to print a clickable file:// URL for the browser-friendly
version.

.PP
Resolution precedence and output-mode details are collected under NOTES.


.SH COMMON WORKFLOW
A typical interactive session signs in, acquires a phone, observes it,
performs an action, verifies the result, and releases the session:

.EX
axilio login
eval "$(axilio sessions start --export)"
axilio phone observe
axilio phone tap --query "the search box"
axilio phone observe
axilio sessions stop <session-id>
.EE

.PP
Use \fBaxilio sessions start --export\fR with \fBeval\fR when separate shells or
agents must pin different sessions through \fBAXILIO_SESSION\fR\&.


.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for API-backed commands; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for API-backed commands; overrides
AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in human-oriented output
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth organization slug or id; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Result format for runnable application
commands: table or json; help, completion, and version stay text, and
sessions start --export stays shell (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes and prompts; destructive
commands still require --yes


.SH COMMANDS
Commands are grouped by their top-level family. Each runnable command
includes representative examples, output, and exit statuses.

.SH api-keys
.EX
axilio api-keys
.EE

.PP
Manage API keys scoped to the active organization. List keys to discover
their IDs, create a named key whose secret is shown once, or delete a
key by ID. Organization access and API-key management permissions are
enforced by the API.

.PP
Running \fBaxilio api-keys\fR without a subcommand is equivalent to \fBaxilio
api-keys --help\fR: it only displays this help and does not list, create,
or delete API keys. Global flags shown here therefore have no effect.
Pass flags to an api-keys subcommand instead.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP, \fB--output\fP
/ \fB-o\fP, \fB--quiet\fP / \fB-q\fP - No effect on api-keys command; bare
axilio api-keys only displays this help

.PP
\fBWorkflow examples\fP

.EX
axilio api-keys list
axilio api-keys create ci
axilio api-keys delete key_123 --yes
.EE

.SS list
.EX
axilio api-keys list
.EE

.PP
List API keys in the active organization.

.PP
Results include key ID, name, masked preview, last-used time, and
creation time. Full secret values are never returned; use the ID with
\fBapi-keys delete\fR\&.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the API-key list request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the API-key list request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
API-key list
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the API-key list request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the API-key list as table or
json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the API-key list
request; the API-key list remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio api-keys list
ID       NAME  KEY       LAST USED  CREATED
<key-id> ci    axl_ci…   -          <timestamp>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Only the masked preview is returned; an empty result says no
#        keys were found.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio api-keys list -o json
{
  "api_keys": [
    {
      "id": "<key-id>",
      "name": "ci",
      "key_preview": "axl_ci…",
      "created_at": "<timestamp>"
    }
  ],
  "limit": 50,
  "offset": 0,
  "total": 1
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Key IDs and timestamps vary; full secrets are never listed.
.EE

.SS create
.EX
axilio api-keys create <name>
.EE

.PP
Create a named API key in the active organization.

.PP
The result includes the ID, name, full secret, and creation time. Save
the secret immediately: later list calls show only a preview and the
full value cannot be retrieved.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the API-key create request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the API-key create request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
created API key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the API-key create request;
overrides AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the created API key as table or
json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the save-now warning; the created key
remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio api-keys create ci
ID       <key-id>
Name     ci
Key      axl_<new-secret>
Created  <timestamp>
.sp
# Standard error:
Save this key now; it will not be shown again.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio api-keys create "release automation" -o json
{
  "id": "<key-id>",
  "name": "release automation",
  "key_value": "axl_<new-secret>",
  "created_at": "<timestamp>"
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SS delete
.EX
axilio api-keys delete <key-id> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Permanently delete an organization API key using an ID discovered with
\fBapi-keys list\fR\&.

.PP
Without --yes, table mode reads confirmation from stdin, including
redirected input. JSON and quiet modes do not prompt and require --yes.
JSON success reports the deleted key ID.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP - Delete without prompting; required in JSON or
quiet mode

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - No effect on api-keys delete command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for API-key deletion; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for API-key deletion; overrides
AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for API-key deletion; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON
API-key deletion result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the API-key deletion prompt and human
result; --yes is still required; JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio api-keys delete key_123
.sp
# Standard error:
Delete API key key_123? [y/N] Deleted key_123
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Without --yes, table mode reads confirmation from stdin,
#        including redirected input. JSON and quiet modes require --yes.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio api-keys delete key_123 --yes
.sp
# Standard error:
Deleted key_123
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SH completion
.EX
axilio completion
.EE

.PP
Generate a shell completion script for axilio.

.PP
After installing the generated completion script, users can type:

.EX
axilio api-<Tab>
axilio phone <Tab>
axilio sessions start --<Tab>
.EE

.PP
Their shell can complete command names, subcommands, and flags, reducing
typos and making the command tree easier to discover. Completion is
currently limited to this static command metadata; Axilio resource IDs
and names are not fetched dynamically.

.PP
Choose bash, zsh, fish, or powershell. The generated script is written
to stdout so it can be sourced for the current shell or redirected to
that shell's completion directory.

.PP
\fBWorkflow examples\fP

.EX
source <(axilio completion bash)
axilio completion zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_axilio"
axilio completion fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/axilio.fish
axilio completion powershell | Out-String | Invoke-Expression
.EE

.SS bash
.EX
axilio completion bash
.EE

.PP
Generate the Bash completion script for axilio.

.PP
Load completions in the current shell:

.EX
source <(axilio completion bash)
.EE

.PP
For future shells, install the script in Bash's completion directory:

.EX
axilio completion bash > /etc/bash_completion.d/axilio
.EE

.PP
On macOS with Homebrew's bash-completion, use:

.EX
axilio completion bash > "$(brew --prefix)/etc/bash_completion.d/axilio"
.EE

.PP
The bash-completion package must be installed and loaded.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-descriptions\fP - disable completion descriptions

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % source <(axilio completion bash)
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Loads completions in the current Bash session.
.EE

.SS fish
.EX
axilio completion fish [flags]
.EE

.PP
Generate the Fish completion script for axilio.

.PP
Install it for future shells:

.EX
axilio completion fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/axilio.fish
.EE

.PP
Fish loads completion files from this directory automatically.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-descriptions\fP - disable completion descriptions

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio completion fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/axilio.fish
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Installs the script where Fish loads it automatically.
.EE

.SS powershell
.EX
axilio completion powershell [flags]
.EE

.PP
Generate the PowerShell completion script for axilio.

.PP
Load completions in the current shell:

.EX
axilio completion powershell | Out-String | Invoke-Expression
.EE

.PP
Add the command to your PowerShell profile to load completions in future
shells.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-descriptions\fP - disable completion descriptions

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio completion powershell | Out-String | Invoke-Expression
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Loads completions in the current PowerShell session.
.EE

.SS zsh
.EX
axilio completion zsh [flags]
.EE

.PP
Generate the Zsh completion script for axilio.

.PP
Enable Zsh completion if needed, then install the script in a directory
on fpath:

.EX
autoload -U compinit; compinit
axilio completion zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_axilio"
.EE

.PP
On macOS with Homebrew, use:

.EX
axilio completion zsh > "$(brew --prefix)/share/zsh/site-functions/_axilio"
.EE

.PP
Start a new shell after installing the script.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-descriptions\fP - disable completion descriptions

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio completion zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_axilio"
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Installs the script for future Zsh sessions; start a new shell
#        after installation.
.EE

.SH config
.EX
axilio config
.EE

.PP
Inspect and edit CLI configuration without hand-editing files. Bare
\fBaxilio config\fR reports the effective API host, API-key authentication
summary, active organization, config path, and sessions directory. The
current summary does not detect a stored OAuth session, so an OAuth-only
login may be shown as auth method \fBnone\fR; \fBstatus\fR verifies effective
credentials. The only editable key is base-url.

.PP
Current ways to change these values are:

.EX
API host         axilio config set base-url [url]
                 axilio config unset base-url
API key          axilio login --api-key [api_key]
                 axilio logout clears saved credentials
Active org       axilio orgs use [org_name]
                 axilio orgs clear
Config path      set XDG_CONFIG_HOME; file is [value]/axilio/config.json
                 (default ~/.config/axilio/config.json)
Sessions dir     set XDG_CONFIG_HOME; directory is [value]/axilio/sessions
                 (default ~/.config/axilio/sessions)
.EE

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Temporarily shows this as the effective API
key source; does not save the new key. Use axilio login --api-key
[api_key] to verify and persist a new key.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Temporarily shows this as the effective API
host; does not save the new host. See the above help content to change
base-url.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable
configuration table
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Temporarily changes the displayed organization;
does not save the selection. Use axilio orgs use [org_name] instead to
persist changes to active org setting.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the configuration summary as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr update notices; the
configuration summary remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio config
API host     https://api.axilio.ai
Auth method  api-key (source: config)
Active org   (session default)
Config file  <config-path>
Sessions dir <sessions-directory>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio config set base-url https://api.axilio.ai
.sp
# Standard error:
Set base-url = https://api.axilio.ai in <config-path>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio config unset base-url
.sp
# Standard error:
Unset base-url in <config-path>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SS set
.EX
axilio config set <key> <value>
.EE

.PP
Set base-url in the shared config file.

.PP
Use an http or https API origin such as https://api.axilio.ai, without
/api/v1 or another path. Validation currently accepts any URL with a
scheme and host, so a different scheme or path is saved even though
requests may then fail. Requests resolve the host from --base-url,
AXILIO_BASE_URL, this saved value, then https://api.axilio.ai.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP - No effect
on config set command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON key,
value, and config-path result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the human config set confirmation; JSON
still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio config set base-url https://api.axilio.ai
.sp
# Standard error:
Set base-url = https://api.axilio.ai in <config-path>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SS unset
.EX
axilio config unset <key>
.EE

.PP
Remove the saved base-url from the shared config file.

.PP
Subsequent requests fall back to --base-url, AXILIO_BASE_URL, then
https://api.axilio.ai. This does not remove credentials.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP - No effect
on config unset command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON key,
unset, and config-path result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the human config unset confirmation;
JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio config unset base-url
.sp
# Standard error:
Unset base-url in <config-path>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SH doctor
.EX
axilio doctor
.EE

.PP
Run a one-shot health check of credentials, authentication, API
connectivity, account balance and plan, CLI version, config path,
sessions directory, and current session.

.PP
Missing or rejected credentials and authenticated connectivity failures
are required failures and make the command exit non-zero. Account, plan,
and local environment rows are informational; without credentials,
connectivity is also informational. Each network check times out after 8
seconds. Use -o json for an overall ok value and the complete checks
array.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for doctor's authenticated checks;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for doctor's authenticated checks;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
doctor report
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for doctor's authenticated checks;
overrides AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the doctor report as table or
json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for doctor's authenticated
checks; the doctor report remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio doctor
CHECK           | STATUS | DETAIL
Authentication  | ok     | method: oauth (browser session)
Credentials     | ok     | oauth session present
Connectivity    | ok     | https://api.axilio.ai/api/v1 reachable
Account         | ok     | balance: $5.00
Plan            | ok     | Hobby (active, up to 1 concurrent)
CLI version     | ok     | 0.6.1 (<commit>) <go-version> <build-date>
Config file     | ok     | <config-path>
Sessions dir    | ok     | <sessions-directory>
Current session | ok     | <session-id> (<phone-id>)
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Representative authenticated report; balance, plan, build
#        metadata, paths, and current session vary.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio doctor -o json
{
  "checks": [
    {
      "name": "Authentication",
      "status": "ok",
      "detail": "method: oauth (browser session)"
    },
    {
      "name": "Credentials",
      "status": "ok",
      "detail": "oauth session present"
    },
    {
      "name": "Connectivity",
      "status": "ok",
      "detail": "https://api.axilio.ai/api/v1 reachable"
    },
    {
      "name": "Account",
      "status": "ok",
      "detail": "balance: $5.00"
    },
    {
      "name": "Plan",
      "status": "ok",
      "detail": "Hobby (active, up to 1 concurrent)"
    },
    {
      "name": "CLI version",
      "status": "ok",
      "detail": "0.6.1 (<commit>) <go-version> <build-date>"
    },
    {
      "name": "Config file",
      "status": "ok",
      "detail": "<config-path>"
    },
    {
      "name": "Sessions dir",
      "status": "ok",
      "detail": "<sessions-directory>"
    },
    {
      "name": "Current session",
      "status": "ok",
      "detail": "<session-id> (<phone-id>)"
    }
  ],
  "ok": true
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: The JSON contains the same checks and representative values as
#        the table; account and local values vary.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % AXILIO_API_KEY=axl_invalid axilio doctor
CHECK          | STATUS | DETAIL
Authentication | ok     | method: api-key (source: env (AXILIO_API_KEY))
Credentials    | ok     | API key present (axl_…)
Connectivity   | ok     | https://api.axilio.ai/api/v1 reachable
Authentication | fail   | API key rejected (HTTP 401); run `axilio login`
\&...
.sp
# Standard error:
doctor: API key rejected (HTTP 401); run `axilio login`
.sp
# Exit status: 3
# Notes: Missing or rejected credentials exit 3. When credentials are
#        configured but the Axilio API cannot be reached, doctor exits
#        6.
.EE

.SH help
.EX
axilio help [command] [flags]
.EE

.PP
Show help for axilio or one of its commands.

.PP
Use --html without a command name to print a clickable file:// URL for
the installed, browser-friendly manual.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--html\fP - Print the file:// URL for the installed HTML manual

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP, \fB--output\fP
/ \fB-o\fP, \fB--quiet\fP / \fB-q\fP - No effect on help command or the help
content it renders

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio help phone tap
Perform a tap action on the selected phone.
.sp
USAGE
.sp
  axilio phone tap [x y] [--flags]
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: The complete help includes examples and command-effective flag
#        descriptions.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio help --html
file:///path/to/axilio.1.html
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: The URL points to the self-contained HTML manual installed with
#        Homebrew or install.sh.
.EE

.SH init
.EX
axilio init [flags]
.EE

.PP
Write an instruction file that teaches your coding agent to drive a
phone through the axilio CLI and then hand back a runnable Python or Go
script using the Axilio SDK. The agent asks whether you want Python or
Go.

.PP
Bare \fBaxilio init\fR detects which agents this repo uses (.claude/,
AGENTS.md, .cursor/) and writes a skill for each; on a terminal with
nothing detected it asks. --agent picks one explicitly:

.EX
--agent claude  ->  .claude/skills/axilio/SKILL.md
--agent codex   ->  AGENTS.md (appended, never clobbered)
--agent cursor  ->  .cursor/rules/axilio.mdc
.EE

.PP
Auto-detected targets that already contain the skill are skipped. An
explicit target that already exists is an error unless --force is set;
for AGENTS.md, --force replaces only the marked Axilio block. Without
markers, interactive mode asks which agent to configure, while JSON,
quiet, or redirected use requires --agent.

.PP
It finishes with a sign-in check: browser login is the one step an agent
can't do itself, so init surfaces it while a human is likely at the
keyboard.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--agent\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Target claude, codex, or cursor; omit to detect
repository markers
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--force\fP - Refresh an existing skill; only the marked Axilio
AGENTS.md block is replaced

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--org\fP - No effect on init command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Host for the skill download and sign-in
check; overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in init success messages
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit human init messages or JSON
written and skipped path lists (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress human init prompts and messages;
--agent may be required; JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio init
.sp
# Standard error:
✓ Wrote the Axilio agent skill to <detected-target>
Not signed in. A human must run `axilio login` (browser), or set AXILIO_API_KEY.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Representative stderr excerpt; detected targets depend on
#        repository markers, existing auto-detected skills may be
#        skipped, and the command finishes with a suggested agent
#        prompt.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio init --agent codex
.sp
# Standard error:
✓ Wrote the Axilio agent skill to AGENTS.md
Not signed in. A human must run `axilio login` (browser), or set AXILIO_API_KEY.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Excerpt: stderr then prints the suggested first agent prompt.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio init --agent claude --force
.sp
# Standard error:
✓ Wrote the Axilio agent skill to .claude/skills/axilio/SKILL.md
Not signed in. A human must run `axilio login` (browser), or set AXILIO_API_KEY.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Excerpt: --force replaces an existing Axilio-owned Claude skill
#        before the suggested first agent prompt.
.EE

.SH login
.EX
axilio login
.EE

.PP
Sign in to Axilio.

.PP
With no arguments on a terminal, open a browser OAuth flow and store the
session in the OS keychain, with a protected file fallback. Pass
--api-key, or pipe a key on stdin, to verify an axl_ API key against the
API and persist it in the shared Axilio config file. A --base-url
supplied with API-key login is saved with the key.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Verify and save this API key instead of
opening browser OAuth
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for login; also saved when API-key
login succeeds
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in login progress and success
messages
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Does not choose the login org; only scopes the
post-login OAuth balance request
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit human login messages or a JSON
sign-in result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress human login messages; browser OAuth
still opens; JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio login
.sp
# Standard error:
→ Opening your browser to authorize the CLI…
✓ Signed in to https://api.axilio.ai
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Representative stderr excerpt; the browser URL, optional
#        organization line, and balance result vary by login.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio login --api-key axl_xxx
.sp
# Standard error:
✓ Signed in to https://api.axilio.ai
  Balance  $5.00
  Saved to <config-path>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: axl_xxx is a non-secret format placeholder; replace it with a
#        valid key before running the command.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % printf '%s\\n' "$AXILIO_API_KEY" | axilio login
.sp
# Standard error:
✓ Signed in to https://api.axilio.ai
  Balance  $5.00
  Saved to <config-path>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SH logout
.EX
axilio logout
.EE

.PP
Sign out locally and, when present, revoke the OAuth refresh-token
family server-side.

.PP
The saved API key, OAuth session, and active organization are removed. A
saved base URL, environment credentials, and locally saved phone-session
files are not removed.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--org\fP - No effect on logout command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the signed-out success message
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human sign-out message or JSON
sign-out result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress human logout warnings and results; JSON
still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio logout
.sp
# Standard error:
✓ Signed out.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Already-signed-out is also exit 0 and reports Already signed
#        out.
.EE

.SH orgs
.EX
axilio orgs
.EE

.PP
Swap between the organizations you belong to without signing in again.

.PP
\fBorgs list\fR shows them, \fBorgs use \\<slug\\>\fR sets the active org for
future commands, and \fB--org\fR / \fBAXILIO_ORG\fR override it for a single
call. API keys are bound to one org, so this applies to \fBaxilio login\fR
(OAuth) sessions.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API-key auth cannot list OAuth memberships;
use a saved OAuth session
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the organization-list request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable organization
listing
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Temporarily changes the organization marked active
in the listing; does not save the selection
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render organizations and the active
selection as table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress orgs stderr notes; the organization
list remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio orgs
SLUG         NAME          ID
*  example-org  Example Inc.  <organization-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio orgs list
SLUG         NAME          ID
*  example-org  Example Inc.  <organization-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio orgs use example-org
.sp
# Standard error:
Active organization set to example-org (Example Inc.).
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 4\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio --org another-org workflows list
WORKFLOW ID   NAME      PLATFORM  STATUS  LAST RUN
<workflow-id> Checkout  android   active  <timestamp>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 5\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio orgs clear
.sp
# Standard error:
Cleared the active organization; using your session default.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SS list
.EX
axilio orgs list
.EE

.PP
List organizations available to the saved OAuth session.

.PP
The table includes slug, name, and ID; \fB*\fR marks the effective active
organization when one is selected. Organization selection resolves from
--org, AXILIO_ORG, \fBorgs use\fR, then the OAuth session default. API-key
logins cannot switch organizations.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API-key auth cannot list OAuth memberships;
use a saved OAuth session
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the organization-list request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable organization
listing
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Temporarily changes the organization marked active
in the listing; does not save the selection
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render organizations and the active
selection as table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress orgs list stderr notes; the
organization list remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio orgs list
SLUG         NAME          ID
*  example-org  Example Inc.  <organization-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio orgs list
SLUG         NAME          ID
   example-org  Example Inc.  <organization-id>
.sp
# Standard error:
No active org set; using your session default. Set one with `axilio orgs use <slug>`.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio orgs list -o json
{
  "active": "example-org",
  "organizations": [
    {"id": "<organization-id>", "slug": "example-org", "name": "Example Inc."}
  ]
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Organization membership and the active selector vary by
#        session.
.EE

.SS clear
.EX
axilio orgs clear
.EE

.PP
Remove the stored active organization.

.PP
OAuth-backed requests then use the organization from AXILIO_ORG or the
OAuth session default unless --org is supplied for the call. This does
not alter API-key scope.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP - No effect
on orgs clear command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON clear
result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the human org-clear confirmation; JSON
still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio orgs clear
.sp
# Standard error:
Cleared the active organization; using your session default.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: If no organization is set, it reports that state and still
#        exits 0.
.EE

.SS use
.EX
axilio orgs use <slug-or-id>
.EE

.PP
Verify a slug or ID against organizations available to the saved OAuth
session, then store its slug as the active organization.

.PP
--org and AXILIO_ORG override this stored selection. API keys remain
bound to their own organization and cannot use this command.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - No effect on orgs use command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API-key auth cannot switch orgs; use a saved
OAuth session
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the membership check; overrides
AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Does not choose the org to save; the positional
slug or ID does
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON
active-organization result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the human org-selection confirmation;
JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio orgs use example-org
.sp
# Standard error:
Active organization set to example-org (Example Inc.).
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SH phone
.EX
axilio phone
.EE

.PP
Drive a phone session started with \fBaxilio sessions start\fR\&.

.PP
A reliable loop is observe the screen, find or semantically target an
element, act, then observe again to verify.

.PP
Available verbs are observe, find, find-text, tap, long-press, swipe,
type, key, screenshot, wait-for, and send. Every successful verb emits a
structured result with -o json.

.PP
Session selection precedence is --session, AXILIO_SESSION, the only
locally saved session, the most recently started session, then an
ambiguity error. Phone command names match the Axilio SDKs, so an
interaction explored in the CLI can be transferred directly into Python
or Go code.

.PP
Running \fBaxilio phone\fR without a subcommand is equivalent to \fBaxilio
phone --help\fR: it only displays this help and does not observe or
control a phone. Phone and global flags shown here therefore have no
effect. Pass flags to a phone subcommand instead.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - No effect on phone command; bare axilio phone
only displays this help

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP, \fB--output\fP
/ \fB-o\fP, \fB--quiet\fP / \fB-q\fP - No effect on phone command; bare axilio
phone only displays this help

.PP
\fBWorkflow examples\fP

.EX
axilio phone observe
axilio phone tap --query "the search box"
axilio phone type "Axilio"
axilio phone observe
.EE

.SS find
.EX
axilio phone find <query> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Locate one visible element from a natural-language description and
return its text, center, bounding box, confidence, and source.

.PP
The OCR engine defaults to free, the vision model is selected by the
server, and the effective deadline is 10 seconds when --timeout is
omitted. A missing target is an error; use \fBfind-text\fR for a successful
empty result.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--model\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Vision model override; omitted lets the server
select the model
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--ocr-engine\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OCR engine: free or premium; omitted uses
free
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--timeout\fP=\fIduration\fP - Maximum vision search time, such as 500ms,
15s, or 1m (default 10s). Units: ns, us/µs, ms, s, m, h.

.PP
\fBParent options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Session ID; overrides AXILIO_SESSION and
automatic session selection

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--org\fP - No effect on phone find
command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
found-element result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the found-element result as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for vision search; the
found-element result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone find "the search box"
Text        Search
Center      540,620
BBox        80,560 920x120
Confidence  0.99
Source      ocr
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone find "settings icon" --ocr-engine premium
Text
Center      900,120
BBox        840,60 120x120
Confidence  0.98
Source      vlm
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Vision-model elements can have no text; coordinates depend on
#        the current frame.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone find "continue button" --timeout 15s -o json
{
  "text": "Continue",
  "center": {"x": 540, "y": 1120},
  "bbox": {"x": 80, "y": 1060, "width": 920, "height": 120},
  "confidence": 0.98,
  "source": "ocr"
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Element content and coordinates depend on the current frame.
.EE

.SS find-text
.EX
axilio phone find-text <text> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Search OCR text without semantic vision.

.PP
By default, match a case-insensitive substring and return the first
element. --exact uses a case-sensitive exact match. No match is
successful: table output prints \fBNo match.\fR and JSON output is null
rather than a not-found error.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--exact\fP - Require a case-sensitive exact match instead of
case-insensitive substring

.PP
\fBParent options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Session ID; overrides AXILIO_SESSION and
automatic session selection

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--org\fP - No effect on phone
find-text command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
text-match result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the text-match result as table
or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for OCR search; the
text-match result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone find-text "sign in"
Text        Sign in
Center      540,1120
BBox        80,1060 920x120
Confidence  0.98
Source      ocr
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: The default is a case-insensitive substring match.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone find-text "Sign in" --exact -o json
{
  "bbox": {
    "x": 80,
    "y": 1060,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 120
  },
  "center": {
    "x": 540,
    "y": 1120
  },
  "confidence": 0.98,
  "text": "Sign in",
  "source": "ocr"
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Exact matching is case-sensitive.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone find-text "settings"
No match.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: No match is success; -o json emits null.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 4\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone find-text "settings" -o json
null
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: No match is a successful literal JSON null.
.EE

.SS key
.EX
axilio phone key <name>
.EE

.PP
Press a named key on the selected phone.

.PP
The only supported named key is \fBenter\fR; back, home, and other key names
are not available.

.PP
\fBParent options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Session ID; overrides AXILIO_SESSION and
automatic session selection

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP - No effect
on phone key command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON key
press result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the human key press result; the phone
action still runs; JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone key enter
.sp
# Standard error:
Pressed enter
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SS long-press
.EX
axilio phone long-press <x> <y> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Press and hold at frame-space pixel coordinates, with (0,0) at the
screen's top-left.

.PP
This command is coordinate-only; use observe or find to inspect the
current frame before choosing a point. The default hold duration is 800
milliseconds.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--duration-ms\fP=\fInumber\fP - How long to hold the coordinate, in
milliseconds (default "800")

.PP
\fBParent options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Session ID; overrides AXILIO_SESSION and
automatic session selection

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP - No effect
on phone long-press command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON
long-press result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the human long-press result; the phone
action still runs; JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone long-press 540 1080
.sp
# Standard error:
Long-pressed 540,1080 for 800ms
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone long-press 540 1080 --duration-ms 1200
.sp
# Standard error:
Long-pressed 540,1080 for 1200ms
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SS observe
.EX
axilio phone observe [flags]
.EE

.PP
Capture and analyze the selected phone's current screen.

.PP
OCR uses the free engine when --ocr-engine is omitted. Table output
lists recognized text with center coordinates and confidence, then
summarizes icons and screen dimensions. JSON returns the complete screen
object, including texts, icons, dimensions, screen hash, and capture
time.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--ocr-engine\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OCR engine: free or premium; omitted uses
free

.PP
\fBParent options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Session ID; overrides AXILIO_SESSION and
automatic session selection

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--org\fP - No effect on phone observe
command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
observation result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the observation result as table
or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for observation; the
observation result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone observe
TEXT          X    Y     CONF
coffee shops  540  620   0.99
Continue      540  1120  0.98
.sp
# Standard error:
2 texts, 0 icons  1080x2400
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: JSON includes texts, icons, dimensions, screen hash, and
#        capture time.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone observe --ocr-engine premium
TEXT          X    Y     CONF
coffee shops  540  620   0.99
Continue      540  1120  0.98
.sp
# Standard error:
2 texts, 0 icons  1080x2400
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Premium OCR changes recognition, not the table shape.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone observe -o json
{
  "texts": [
    {"text": "Continue", "center": {"x": 540, "y": 1120}, "confidence": 0.98}
  ],
  "icons": [],
  "hash": "<screen-hash>",
  "width": 1080,
  "height": 2400,
  "captured_at": "<timestamp>"
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Shortened representative screen JSON; elements also include
#        bounding boxes and sources.
.EE

.PP
\fBWalkthrough\fP

.EX
+----------------------------+
| Search                     |
| [ coffee shops           ] |  text "coffee shops"  540,620  0.99
|                            |
| [        Continue        ] |  text "Continue"     540,1120  0.98
+----------------------------+
right-side fields: text, center (x,y), confidence
frame 1080x2400; frame-space pixels; (0,0) is top-left
.sp
reuse the observed Continue center:
axilio phone tap 540 1120
.EE

.SS screenshot
.EX
axilio phone screenshot [flags]
.EE

.PP
Capture the selected phone's screen as PNG bytes and write them to
--out.

.PP
The default destination is screenshot.png in the current directory. If
the destination already exists, its contents are overwritten without
confirmation; the CLI does not create a backup. On success the human
result reports the path and byte count.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--out\fP=\fIvalue\fP - PNG path to create; overwrite existing contents
without confirmation (default "screenshot.png")

.PP
\fBParent options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Session ID; overrides AXILIO_SESSION and
automatic session selection

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP - No effect
on phone screenshot command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON
screenshot write result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the human screenshot result; the phone
action still runs; JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone screenshot
.sp
# Standard error:
Wrote screenshot.png (<bytes> bytes)
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: A new file requests mode 0644, subject to the process umask.
#        Overwriting an existing file preserves its mode while replacing
#        its contents.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone screenshot --out login.png
.sp
# Standard error:
Wrote login.png (<bytes> bytes)
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: A new file requests mode 0644, subject to the process umask.
#        Overwriting an existing file preserves its mode while replacing
#        its contents.
.EE

.SS send
.EX
axilio phone send <path> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Upload a local file into the org library and push it into the phone's
media library so it appears in the gallery.

.PP
Targets the current session's phone (override with --session). Supported
images are jpg, jpeg, png, webp, gif, and heic; supported videos are
mp4, webm, mov, 3gp, and mkv. The target collection is inferred by media
type unless DCIM, Pictures, or Movies is selected. Phones accept
deliveries up to 100 MiB. By default the command returns after dispatch;
--wait blocks for delivered or failed, and --timeout applies only with
--wait. This combines \fBuploads add\fR and \fBuploads push\fR and therefore
retains the upload in the org library.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--collection\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Target DCIM, Pictures, or Movies; omitted
infers from media type
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--timeout\fP=\fIduration\fP - Maximum delivery wait, such as 30s, 1m30s,
or 2m; applies only with --wait (default 1m). Units: ns, us/µs, ms, s,
m, h.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--wait\fP - Block until the phone reports delivered or failed instead
of returning at dispatch

.PP
\fBParent options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Session ID; overrides AXILIO_SESSION and
automatic session selection

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the upload-and-delivery request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the upload-and-delivery request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
delivery result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the upload-and-delivery request;
overrides AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the delivery result as table or
json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress upload progress and delivery notes; the
delivery result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone send ./photo.jpg
Delivery  <delivery-id>
File      photo.jpg
Status    dispatched
.sp
# Standard error:
→ Sending photo.jpg to phone <phone-id>
pushed without requesting delivery receipt. In the future, add --wait if you want the cli to wait for delivery confirmation and report result.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: The upload remains in the organization library.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone send ./clip.mp4 --collection Movies
Delivery  <delivery-id>
File      clip.mp4
Status    dispatched
.sp
# Standard error:
→ Sending clip.mp4 to phone <phone-id>
pushed without requesting delivery receipt. In the future, add --wait if you want the cli to wait for delivery confirmation and report result.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: The upload remains in the organization library and is delivered
#        to Movies.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone send ./photo.jpg --wait --timeout 2m
Delivery  <delivery-id>
File      photo.jpg
Status    delivered
.sp
# Standard error:
→ Sending photo.jpg to phone <phone-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: With --wait, the command returns only after delivered, failed,
#        or the two-minute deadline.
.EE

.SS swipe
.EX
axilio phone swipe <x1> <y1> <x2> <y2> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Swipe between two frame-space pixel coordinates, with (0,0) at the
screen's top-left.

.PP
This command is coordinate-only; use observe to inspect the current
frame. The default gesture duration is 300 milliseconds.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--duration-ms\fP=\fInumber\fP - How long the swipe gesture takes, in
milliseconds (default "300")

.PP
\fBParent options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Session ID; overrides AXILIO_SESSION and
automatic session selection

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP - No effect
on phone swipe command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON swipe
result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the human swipe result; the phone
action still runs; JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone swipe 540 1600 540 500
.sp
# Standard error:
Swiped 540,1600 -> 540,500
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone swipe 200 800 900 800 --duration-ms 500
.sp
# Standard error:
Swiped 200,800 -> 900,800
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SS tap
.EX
axilio phone tap [x y] [flags]
.EE

.PP
Perform a tap action on the selected phone.

.PP
The coordinate form takes x and y as frame-space pixels, with (0,0) at
the screen's top-left.

.PP
Use --query to find an element by natural-language description and tap
its center. If --query and coordinates are both provided, --query takes
precedence.

.PP
Session selection precedence is --session, AXILIO_SESSION, the only
locally saved session, the most recently started session, then an
ambiguity error.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--model\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Vision model for --query only; omitted lets the
server select
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--ocr-engine\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OCR engine for --query only: free or
premium; omitted uses free
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--query\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Recommended natural-language target; vision
finds it and taps its center

.PP
\fBParent options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Session ID; overrides AXILIO_SESSION and
automatic session selection

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP - No effect
on phone tap command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON tap
result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the human tap result; the phone action
still runs; JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone tap --query "the search box"
.sp
# Standard error:
Tapped "the search box" at 540,620
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone tap 540 1200
.sp
# Standard error:
Tapped 540,1200
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone tap --session sess_123 --query "continue"
.sp
# Standard error:
Tapped "continue" at 540,1120
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SS type
.EX
axilio phone type <text>
.EE

.PP
Type text into the focused field on the selected phone.

.PP
Enclose text in quotes when it contains spaces or shell-special
characters. Text is entered through a US-layout keyboard. Printable
ASCII characters are supported; emoji and other non-ASCII characters are
silently skipped.

.PP
\fBParent options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Session ID; overrides AXILIO_SESSION and
automatic session selection

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP - No effect
on phone type command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON
typing result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the human typing result; the phone
action still runs; JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone type "hello world"
.sp
# Standard error:
Typed "hello world"
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone type 'user@example.com'
.sp
# Standard error:
Typed "user@example.com"
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone type "don't split this text"
.sp
# Standard error:
Typed "don't split this text"
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SS wait-for
.EX
axilio phone wait-for <text> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Poll OCR until text appears, or until it disappears with --gone.

.PP
The default match is a case-insensitive substring; --exact requires a
case-sensitive exact match. The default timeout is 10 seconds. A timeout
returns the CLI timeout exit code (5). Waiting for presence returns the
matching element; waiting for absence is action-only.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--exact\fP - Require a case-sensitive exact match instead of
substring
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--gone\fP - Wait for the text to disappear instead of appear
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--timeout\fP=\fIduration\fP - Maximum OCR polling time, such as 500ms,
10s, or 1m; exceeding it exits 5 (default 10s). Units: ns, us/µs, ms, s,
m, h.

.PP
\fBParent options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--session\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Session ID; overrides AXILIO_SESSION and
automatic session selection

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--org\fP - No effect on phone wait-for
command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
matched-element result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render a present match or --gone result
as table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress human wait notes; table or JSON results
remain on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone wait-for "Results"
Text        Results
Center      540,1120
BBox        80,1060 920x120
Confidence  0.98
Source      ocr
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone wait-for "Loading" --gone
.sp
# Standard error:
"Loading" gone
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone wait-for "Ready" --exact --timeout 30s
Text        Ready
Center      540,1120
BBox        80,1060 920x120
Confidence  0.98
Source      ocr
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Exact matching is case-sensitive and waits up to 30 seconds.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 4\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phone wait-for "Results" --timeout 1s
.sp
# Standard error:
timeout: text not found within deadline: Results
.sp
# Exit status: 5
# Notes: A wait timeout exits 5.
.EE

.SH phones
.EX
axilio phones
.EE

.PP
Discover phones before starting a session. \fBphones list\fR shows shared
phones and currently free dedicated phones that can be allocated now.
\fBphones mine\fR shows the organization's complete dedicated inventory,
including busy and offline phones, and is the place to find a phone ID
for \fBsessions start --phone-id\fR\&.

.PP
Running \fBaxilio phones\fR without a subcommand is equivalent to \fBaxilio
phones --help\fR: it only displays this help and does not list or change
phones. Global flags shown here therefore have no effect. Pass flags to
\fBphones list\fR or \fBphones mine\fR instead.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP, \fB--output\fP
/ \fB-o\fP, \fB--quiet\fP / \fB-q\fP - No effect on phones command; bare
axilio phones only displays this help

.PP
\fBWorkflow examples\fP

.EX
axilio phones list
axilio phones mine
.EE

.SS list
.EX
axilio phones list
.EE

.PP
List the phones available to start a session on immediately: every
active phone in the shared pool, plus your org's own dedicated phones
that are currently free.

.PP
Busy or offline dedicated phones do not appear here; use \fBaxilio phones
mine\fR to see the full dedicated inventory. Results include phone ID,
type, model, and status.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the available-phone request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the available-phone request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
available-phone result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the available-phone request;
overrides AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the available-phone result as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the available-phone
request; the available-phone result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phones list
PHONE ID   TYPE     MODEL    STATUS
<phone-id> android  Pixel 8  active
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: An empty successful result prints No phones available.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phones list -o json
{
  "android_count": 1,
  "iphone_count": 0,
  "phones": [
    {
      "created_at": "<timestamp>",
      "model_name": "Pixel 8",
      "ownership_type": "shared",
      "phone_id": "<phone-id>",
      "phone_type": "android",
      "status": "active",
      "updated_at": "<timestamp>"
    }
  ]
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Counts, inventory, and optional phone fields vary by
#        organization and availability.
.EE

.SS mine
.EX
axilio phones mine
.EE

.PP
List your organization's full dedicated (private/rented) phone inventory
in every state - free, busy in an active session, or offline.

.PP
This is how you discover a phone_id to pin with \fBaxilio sessions start
--phone-id\fR\&. Results include phone ID, nickname, type, model, status,
and the session ID holding a busy phone.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the dedicated-phone request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the dedicated-phone request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
dedicated-phone result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the dedicated-phone request;
overrides AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the dedicated-phone result as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the dedicated-phone
request; the dedicated-phone result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio phones mine
PHONE ID   NICKNAME  TYPE     MODEL    STATUS  SESSION
<phone-id> demo      android  Pixel 8  active  <session-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: An empty successful result prints No dedicated phones.
.EE

.SH runs
.EX
axilio runs
.EE

.PP
Manage workflow executions in the active organization. Discover a
workflow ID with \fBworkflows list\fR, start one or more runs, list recent
run IDs and statuses, inspect a run in detail, or cancel queued and
running work.

.PP
Running \fBaxilio runs\fR without a subcommand is equivalent to \fBaxilio runs
--help\fR: it only displays this help and does not list, start, inspect,
or cancel runs. Global flags shown here therefore have no effect. Pass
flags to a runs subcommand instead.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP, \fB--output\fP
/ \fB-o\fP, \fB--quiet\fP / \fB-q\fP - No effect on runs command; bare axilio
runs only displays this help

.PP
\fBWorkflow examples\fP

.EX
axilio workflows list
axilio runs start wf_123
axilio runs list --workflow wf_123
axilio runs get run_123
.EE

.SS list
.EX
axilio runs list [flags]
.EE

.PP
List recent runs in the active organization, most recent first.

.PP
Filter by workflow ID and cap the result count with --limit. Table rows
include run ID, status, trigger, workflow ID, and creation time; use a
returned run ID with \fBruns get\fR or \fBruns cancel\fR\&.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--limit\fP=\fInumber\fP - Maximum number of most-recent runs to return
(default "20")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--workflow\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Return only runs for this workflow ID

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the run-list request; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the run-list request; overrides
AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
run-list result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the run-list request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the run-list result as table or
json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the run-list request;
the run-list result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs list
RUN ID   STATUS     TRIGGER  WORKFLOW      CREATED
<run-id> completed  manual   <workflow-id> <timestamp>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: An empty successful result prints No runs found.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs list --workflow wf_123 --limit 10
RUN ID   STATUS     TRIGGER  WORKFLOW  CREATED
<run-id> completed  manual   wf_123    <timestamp>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Run IDs, statuses, and timestamps vary.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs list -o json
{
  "limit": 20,
  "offset": 0,
  "runs": [
    {
      "id": "<run-id>",
      "status": "completed",
      "trigger": "manual",
      "workflow_id": "<workflow-id>"
    }
  ],
  "total": 1
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Shortened representative JSON output; run records may include
#        additional fields.
.EE

.SS cancel
.EX
axilio runs cancel <run-id> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Cancel a queued or running run by an ID discovered with \fBruns list\fR\&.

.PP
Without --yes, table mode reads confirmation from stdin, including
redirected input. JSON and quiet modes do not prompt and require --yes.
JSON success reports the canceled run ID.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP - Cancel without prompting; required in JSON or
quiet mode

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - No effect on runs cancel command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for run cancellation; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for run cancellation; overrides
AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for run cancellation; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON run
cancellation result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the run cancellation prompt and human
result; --yes is still required; JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs cancel run_123
.sp
# Standard error:
Cancel run run_123? [y/N] Canceled run_123
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Without --yes, table mode reads confirmation from stdin,
#        including redirected input. JSON and quiet modes require --yes.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs cancel run_123 --yes
.sp
# Standard error:
Canceled run_123
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SS get
.EX
axilio runs get <run-id>
.EE

.PP
Fetch one run by the ID returned from \fBruns list\fR or \fBruns start\fR\&.

.PP
The result includes status, trigger, workflow, session, phone, created,
started and completed times, error message, and video URL when present.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the run-detail request; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the run-detail request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
run-detail result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the run-detail request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the run-detail result as table
or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the run-detail
request; the run-detail result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs get run_123
Run        run_123
Status     completed
Trigger    manual
Workflow   <workflow-id>
Session    <session-id>
Phone      <phone-id>
Created    <created-at>
Started    <started-at>
Completed  <completed-at>
Error      -
Video      <video-url>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs get run_123 -o json
{
  "id": "run_123",
  "status": "completed",
  "trigger": "manual",
  "workflow_id": "<workflow-id>",
  "session_id": "<session-id>",
  "phone_id": "<phone-id>"
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Shortened representative JSON output; timestamps, errors, and
#        video URL appear when available.
.EE

.SS start
.EX
axilio runs start <workflow-id> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Create runs for a workflow ID discovered with \fBworkflows list\fR\&.

.PP
--count creates that many run configurations; v0.5.0 does not validate
its range locally, so use a positive count.

.PP
--phone-id pins every created run to a specific dedicated phone.

.PP
--start-timeout is the number of whole seconds a queued run may wait for
a phone before auto-cancel. Positive values are sent to the server,
which may reject unsupported values; zero or negative values omit the
field and use the server default.

.PP
Successful output contains the created run IDs.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--count\fP=\fInumber\fP - Number of run configurations to create; v0.5.0
does not validate the range (default "1")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--phone-id\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Dedicated phone ID to pin to every created
run
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--start-timeout\fP=\fInumber\fP - Queued-phone wait in whole seconds,
such as 30, 300, or 900; positive values are sent to the server, while 0
or negative values use the server default

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - No effect on runs start command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the run-create request; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the run-create request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the run-create request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit created run IDs as human messages
or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress table-mode run IDs and guidance; a JSON
result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs start wf_123
.sp
# Standard error:
Started run <run-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: -o json emits the complete run_ids response on stdout.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs start wf_123 --count 3
.sp
# Standard error:
Started run <run-id-1>
Started run <run-id-2>
Started run <run-id-3>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs start wf_123 --phone-id ph_123
.sp
# Standard error:
Started run <run-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 4\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio runs start wf_123 --start-timeout 300
.sp
# Standard error:
Started run <run-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SH sessions
.EX
axilio sessions
.EE

.PP
Manage the phone sessions used by \fBaxilio phone\fR\&. Sessions remain active
in Axilio until stopped; the CLI saves connection information locally so
later phone commands can reconnect. Session selection precedence is
--session, AXILIO_SESSION, the only locally saved session, the most
recently started session, then an ambiguity error. \fBsessions list
--remote\fR asks the API for all active Axilio sessions, including
sessions not saved on this computer.

.PP
Running \fBaxilio sessions\fR without a subcommand is equivalent to \fBaxilio
sessions --help\fR: it only displays this help and does not acquire, list,
select, or stop sessions. Global flags shown here therefore have no
effect. Pass flags to a sessions subcommand instead.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP, \fB--output\fP
/ \fB-o\fP, \fB--quiet\fP / \fB-q\fP - No effect on sessions command; bare
axilio sessions only displays this help

.PP
\fBWorkflow examples\fP

.EX
axilio sessions list
axilio sessions start
axilio sessions current
axilio sessions stop sess_123
.EE

.SS list
.EX
axilio sessions list [flags]
.EE

.PP
List sessions saved locally by default.

.PP
The \fB*\fR marker identifies the session that phone commands would select
in this shell when selection is not ambiguous. Use --remote to list all
active Axilio sessions instead; remote rows include session ID, phone
ID, phone type, and model but do not indicate which session this CLI
would select.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--remote\fP - List all active Axilio sessions instead of sessions
saved locally

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Authenticates only --remote listing; no effect
on sessions saved locally
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Selects the API host only with --remote; no
effect on sessions saved locally
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable session
listing
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Selects the OAuth org only with --remote; no
effect on sessions saved locally
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render local or remote sessions as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes; the session listing
remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions list
SESSION       PHONE       TYPE
*  <session-id>  <phone-id>  android
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: With no sessions saved locally, stdout explains how to start
#        one and exit status is 0.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions list --remote
SESSION       PHONE       TYPE     MODEL
<session-id>  <phone-id>  android  Pixel 8
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Remote results come from the API and do not mark the session
#        selected by this CLI.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions list -o json
[
  {
    "session_id": "<session-id>",
    "phone_id": "<phone-id>",
    "phone_type": "android",
    "control_url": "<control-url>",
    "created_at": "<timestamp>"
  }
]
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Locally saved session JSON includes the stored control URL; IDs
#        and URLs vary.
.EE

.SS current
.EX
axilio sessions current
.EE

.PP
Resolve and show the session selected for phone commands.

.PP
Phone command session selection precedence is --session, AXILIO_SESSION,
the only locally saved session, the most recently started session, then
an ambiguity error. This command has no --session flag, so it starts at
AXILIO_SESSION. If no session is selected, the command prints a note and
exits 0.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--org\fP - No effect on sessions
current command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
current-session result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the current-session result as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for session resolution;
the current-session result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions current
Session  <session-id>
Phone    <phone-id>
Type     android
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: No selected session is an exit-0 answer; JSON prints null.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % AXILIO_SESSION=sess_123 axilio sessions current
Session  sess_123
Phone    <phone-id>
Type     android
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: The named session must be saved locally; AXILIO_SESSION takes
#        precedence over automatic session selection.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions current -o json
{
  "session_id": "<session-id>",
  "phone_id": "<phone-id>",
  "phone_type": "android",
  "control_url": "<control-url>",
  "created_at": "<timestamp>"
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: With no selected session, the successful JSON result is null.
.EE

.SS start
.EX
axilio sessions start [flags]
.EE

.PP
Acquire an Android phone by default.

.PP
The session remains active in Axilio until stopped; the CLI saves its
connection information locally and marks it as the most recently started
session. Select iphone with --phone-type, pin a dedicated phone
discovered through \fBphones mine\fR with --phone-id, or attach the session
to a workflow with --workflow. --export prints only \fBexport
AXILIO_SESSION=\\<id\\>\fR for shell eval; that shell syntax also wins when
-o json is supplied.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--export\fP - Print only \fBexport AXILIO_SESSION=\\<id\\>\fR for shell
eval
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--phone-id\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Pin a dedicated phone ID from \fBphones mine\fR
instead of pool allocation
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--phone-type\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Phone platform to allocate: android or
iphone (default "android")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--workflow\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Workflow ID to attach; omit for an
interactive session

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the phone-allocation request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the phone-allocation request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
allocated-session result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the phone-allocation request;
overrides AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the allocated session as table
or json; --export always emits shell text (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress session guidance; the result or
--export text remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions start
Session      <session-id>
Phone        <phone-id>
Region       us-central
Live view    <live-view-url>
Control URL  <control-url>
.sp
# Standard error:
Drive it:  axilio phone observe
Pin it to this shell (for parallel work):  export AXILIO_SESSION=<session-id>
Release it with:  axilio sessions stop <session-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions start --phone-type iphone
Session      <session-id>
Phone        <phone-id>
Region       us-central
Live view    <live-view-url>
Control URL  <control-url>
.sp
# Standard error:
Drive it:  axilio phone observe
Pin it to this shell (for parallel work):  export AXILIO_SESSION=<session-id>
Release it with:  axilio sessions stop <session-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions start --phone-id ph_123
Session      <session-id>
Phone        ph_123
Region       us-central
Live view    <live-view-url>
Control URL  <control-url>
.sp
# Standard error:
Drive it:  axilio phone observe
Pin it to this shell (for parallel work):  export AXILIO_SESSION=<session-id>
Release it with:  axilio sessions stop <session-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 4\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions start --workflow wf_123
Session      <session-id>
Phone        <phone-id>
Region       us-central
Live view    <live-view-url>
Control URL  <control-url>
.sp
# Standard error:
Drive it:  axilio phone observe
Pin it to this shell (for parallel work):  export AXILIO_SESSION=<session-id>
Release it with:  axilio sessions stop <session-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 5\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions start --export
export AXILIO_SESSION=<session-id>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: --export emits shell text even when -o json is also supplied.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 6\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % eval "$(axilio sessions start --export)"
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: The shell consumes the nested command's export line and sets
#        AXILIO_SESSION in the current shell.
.EE

.SS stop
.EX
axilio sessions stop <session-id|phone-id> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Release an active phone allocation using either its session ID or phone
ID.

.PP
Discover IDs with \fBsessions list --remote\fR; matching locally saved
session information and the most-recent-session marker are removed after
release. Without --yes, table mode reads confirmation from stdin,
including redirected input. JSON and quiet modes do not prompt and
require --yes.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP - Release without prompting; required in JSON or
quiet mode

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - No effect on sessions stop command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for session release; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for session release; overrides
AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for session release; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON
session release result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the session release prompt and human
result; --yes is still required; JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions stop sess_123
.sp
# Standard error:
Release <phone-id>? [y/N] Released <phone-id>.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Without --yes, table mode reads confirmation from stdin,
#        including redirected input. JSON and quiet modes require --yes.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio sessions stop ph_123 --yes
.sp
# Standard error:
Released ph_123.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SH status
.EX
axilio status
.EE

.PP
Make an authenticated API request and report status, effective API host,
active organization selector, and account balance.

.PP
A valid API key or OAuth session is required. Use -o json for the
structured status, api_host, active_org, and balance fields.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the status request; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the status request; overrides
AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
status result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the status request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the status result as table or
json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the status request;
the status result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio status
Status      ok
API host    https://api.axilio.ai/api/v1
Active org  (session default)
Balance     $5.00
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio status -o json
{
  "active_org": "",
  "api_host": "https://api.axilio.ai/api/v1",
  "balance": "$5.00",
  "status": "ok"
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Balance and active organization vary by account.
.EE

.SH upgrade
.EX
axilio upgrade [flags]
.EE

.PP
Download the latest release from GitHub and replace this binary in place
(the download is checksum-verified).

.PP
Homebrew installs defer to \fBbrew upgrade\fR, and development or \fBgo
install\fR builds are left to the Go toolchain. On a standalone release,
--check reports whether a newer release exists without installing it. A
Homebrew invocation currently prints \fBbrew upgrade axilio\fR guidance and
returns before checking, even when --check is supplied.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--check\fP - Check a standalone release without installing; Homebrew
currently prints upgrade guidance

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP - No effect
on upgrade command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit human upgrade guidance or a JSON
upgrade-status result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress human upgrade guidance and status; JSON
still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio upgrade --check
.sp
# Standard error:
A newer release is available: <old> -> <new>. Run `axilio upgrade` to install.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: The version placeholders vary. This is the newer-release
#        branch; up-to-date, no-release, development, and
#        Homebrew-managed installations report their own state instead.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio upgrade
.sp
# Standard error:
Upgrading axilio <current-version> -> <latest-version>...
Upgraded to <latest-version>.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Standalone release only; development builds and
#        Homebrew-managed installs print their own package-manager
#        guidance.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % brew upgrade axilio
.sp
# External behavior: Output and exit status are owned by Homebrew, not
#                    the axilio CLI.
.EE

.SH uploads
.EX
axilio uploads
.EE

.PP
Manage the org file library. Files live here until deleted and can be
pushed to any phone the org holds, so one upload serves many phones.
\fBadd\fR stores a local file, \fBlist\fR discovers uploads and quota, \fBpush\fR
delivers a stored upload, and \fBdelete\fR frees library quota. \fBphone send\fR
combines add and push for the selected session's phone.

.PP
Running \fBaxilio uploads\fR without a subcommand is equivalent to \fBaxilio
uploads --help\fR: it only displays this help and does not add, list,
push, or delete uploads. Global flags shown here therefore have no
effect. Pass flags to an uploads subcommand instead.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP, \fB--output\fP
/ \fB-o\fP, \fB--quiet\fP / \fB-q\fP - No effect on uploads command; bare
axilio uploads only displays this help

.PP
\fBWorkflow examples\fP

.EX
axilio uploads list
axilio uploads add ./photo.jpg
axilio uploads push upl_123 --phone-id ph_123
axilio uploads delete upl_123 --yes
.EE

.SS list
.EX
axilio uploads list [flags]
.EE

.PP
List uploads and standing storage quota for the active organization.

.PP
Results include upload ID, filename, size, MIME type, status, and
creation time. Page with --limit and --offset, search filenames by
case-insensitive substring, and sort by created_at, filename, or
size_bytes in asc or desc order. Omitting sort/order uses server
defaults.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--limit\fP=\fInumber\fP - Maximum files in this page (default "50")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--offset\fP=\fInumber\fP - Number of matching files to skip before this
page
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--order\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Sort direction: asc or desc; omitted uses server
default
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--search\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Filter filenames by case-insensitive substring
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--sort\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Sort key: created_at, filename, or size_bytes;
omitted uses server default

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the upload-list request; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the upload-list request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
upload-list result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the upload-list request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the upload-list result as table
or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the upload-list
request; the upload-list result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads list
ID          FILENAME   SIZE     TYPE        STATUS  CREATED
<upload-id> photo.jpg  2.0 MiB  image/jpeg  ready   <timestamp>
.sp
# Standard error:
1 of 10000 files, 2.0 MiB of 50.0 GiB used
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: An empty page still reports quota usage; the current global
#        limits are 10000 files and 50 GiB.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads list --search receipt --limit 20 --offset 0
ID          FILENAME     SIZE      TYPE       STATUS  CREATED
<upload-id> receipt.jpg  512.0 KiB image/jpeg ready   <timestamp>
.sp
# Standard error:
1 of 10000 files, 512.0 KiB of 50.0 GiB used
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Results and bytes used vary by organization; the limits are
#        global.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads list --sort filename --order asc
ID          FILENAME   SIZE     TYPE        STATUS  CREATED
<upload-id> photo.jpg  2.0 MiB  image/jpeg  ready   <timestamp>
.sp
# Standard error:
1 of 10000 files, 2.0 MiB of 50.0 GiB used
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Rows are sorted by filename ascending; results and bytes used
#        vary by organization.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 4\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads list -o json
{
  "files": [
    {
      "id": "<upload-id>",
      "filename": "photo.jpg",
      "size_bytes": 2097152,
      "mime_type": "image/jpeg",
      "status": "ready",
      "created_at": "<timestamp>"
    }
  ],
  "total": 1,
  "usage": {
    "file_count": 1,
    "file_limit": 10000,
    "total_bytes": 2097152,
    "byte_limit": 53687091200
  }
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Representative response; files, result count, and bytes used
#        vary by organization; limits are global.
.EE

.SS add
.EX
axilio uploads add <path> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Register a local file, upload its bytes, and verify them, leaving a
ready file in the library.

.PP
Use \fBaxilio uploads push\fR to send it to a phone, or \fBaxilio phone send\fR
to do both in one step. The stored filename defaults to the local
basename and MIME type is inferred from the extension; --filename and
--mime-type override those values.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--filename\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Stored filename; omitted uses the local
file's basename
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--mime-type\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Stored MIME type; omitted infers it from the
file extension

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the file-upload request; overrides
AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the file-upload request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
stored-upload result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the file-upload request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the stored-upload result as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress upload progress; the stored-upload
result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads add ./photo.jpg
ID        <upload-id>
Filename  photo.jpg
Size      2.0 MiB
Type      image/jpeg
Status    ready
.sp
# Standard error:
→ Uploading photo.jpg
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads add ./asset --filename photo.jpg --mime-type image/jpeg
ID        <upload-id>
Filename  photo.jpg
Size      2.0 MiB
Type      image/jpeg
Status    ready
.sp
# Standard error:
→ Uploading asset
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: --filename and --mime-type override values inferred from the
#        local path.
.EE

.SS delete
.EX
axilio uploads delete <upload-id> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Delete an upload from the active organization's library and free its
storage quota.

.PP
Use \fBuploads list\fR to discover the upload ID. Deletion also schedules
removal from every phone holding or receiving a copy. Without --yes,
table mode reads confirmation from stdin, including redirected input.
JSON and quiet modes do not prompt and require --yes. The alias \fBuploads
rm\fR performs the same operation.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP - Delete without prompting; required in JSON or
quiet mode

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - No effect on uploads delete command
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the upload-delete request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the upload-delete request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the upload-delete request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Emit a human confirmation or JSON
deletion result (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress the prompt and human confirmation;
--yes is required; JSON still prints

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads delete upl_123
.sp
# Standard error:
Delete upload upl_123? Also recall it from phones holding or receiving a copy?
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: The table-mode prompt continues with [y/N], then reports
#        Deleted upl_123 after confirmation. Redirected stdin can
#        answer; JSON and quiet modes require --yes.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads rm upl_123 --yes
.sp
# Standard error:
Deleted upl_123
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.SS push
.EX
axilio uploads push <upload-id> [flags]
.EE

.PP
Send a stored library file to a phone's media library.

.PP
Unlike \fBaxilio phone send\fR this uploads nothing, so the same file can be
pushed to many phones without re-uploading it or consuming more quota.
--phone-id is required and can be discovered with \fBphones mine\fR or
\fBsessions list --remote\fR\&. The collection is inferred unless DCIM,
Pictures, or Movies is selected. By default the command returns after
dispatch; --wait blocks for delivered or failed, and --timeout applies
only with --wait.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--collection\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Target DCIM, Pictures, or Movies; omitted
infers from media type
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--phone-id\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Target phone ID from \fBphones mine\fR or remote
sessions (required)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--timeout\fP=\fIduration\fP - Maximum delivery wait, such as 30s, 1m30s,
or 2m; applies only with --wait (default 1m). Units: ns, us/µs, ms, s,
m, h.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--wait\fP - Block until the phone reports delivered or failed instead
of returning at dispatch

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the file-delivery request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the file-delivery request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
delivery result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the file-delivery request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the delivery result as table or
json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress delivery progress and notes; the
delivery result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads push upl_123 --phone-id ph_123
Delivery  <delivery-id>
File      photo.jpg
Status    dispatched
.sp
# Standard error:
→ Pushing upl_123 to phone ph_123
pushed without requesting delivery receipt. In the future, add --wait if you want the cli to wait for delivery confirmation and report result.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads push upl_123 --phone-id ph_123 --collection Pictures
Delivery  <delivery-id>
File      photo.jpg
Status    dispatched
.sp
# Standard error:
→ Pushing upl_123 to phone ph_123
pushed without requesting delivery receipt. In the future, add --wait if you want the cli to wait for delivery confirmation and report result.
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: The phone receives the file in Pictures.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio uploads push upl_123 --phone-id ph_123 --wait --timeout 2m
Delivery  <delivery-id>
File      photo.jpg
Status    delivered
.sp
# Standard error:
→ Pushing upl_123 to phone ph_123
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: With --wait, the command returns only after delivered, failed,
#        or the two-minute deadline.
.EE

.SH workflows
.EX
axilio workflows
.EE

.PP
Inspect workflows in the active organization. Use \fBworkflows list\fR to
discover a workflow ID, then pass that ID to \fBruns start\fR or \fBsessions
start --workflow\fR\&.

.PP
Running \fBaxilio workflows\fR without a subcommand is equivalent to \fBaxilio
workflows --help\fR: it only displays this help and does not list
workflows. Global flags shown here therefore have no effect. Pass flags
to \fBworkflows list\fR instead.

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP, \fB--base-url\fP, \fB--no-color\fP, \fB--org\fP, \fB--output\fP
/ \fB-o\fP, \fB--quiet\fP / \fB-q\fP - No effect on workflows command; bare
axilio workflows only displays this help

.PP
\fBWorkflow examples\fP

.EX
axilio workflows list
axilio workflows list --search checkout
axilio runs start wf_123
.EE

.SS list
.EX
axilio workflows list [flags]
.EE

.PP
List workflows in the active organization, most recent first.

.PP
Results include workflow ID, name, platform, status, and last-run time.
Use --search for a name substring and --limit to control the number
returned. A listed workflow ID can be passed directly to \fBruns start\fR\&.

.PP
\fBCommand options\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--limit\fP=\fInumber\fP - Maximum number of most-recent workflows to
return (default "20")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--search\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Filter workflow names by substring

.PP
\fBGlobal-option behavior\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--api-key\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API key for the workflow-list request;
overrides AXILIO_API_KEY and the saved key
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--base-url\fP=\fIvalue\fP - API host for the workflow-list request;
overrides AXILIO_BASE_URL and saved base-url
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--no-color\fP - Disable ANSI color in the human-readable form of the
workflow-list result
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--org\fP=\fIvalue\fP - OAuth org for the workflow-list request; overrides
AXILIO_ORG and the saved active org; API keys ignore it
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=\fIvalue\fP - Render the workflow-list result as
table or json (default "table")
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP - Suppress stderr notes for the workflow-list
request; the workflow-list result remains on stdout

.PP
\fBExamples and expected output\fP

.PP
\fBSample 1\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows list
WORKFLOW ID   NAME      PLATFORM  STATUS  LAST RUN
<workflow-id> Checkout  android   active  <timestamp>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: An empty successful result prints No workflows found.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 2\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows list --search checkout --limit 10
WORKFLOW ID   NAME      PLATFORM  STATUS  LAST RUN
<workflow-id> Checkout  android   active  <timestamp>
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Names, IDs, statuses, and timestamps vary by organization.
.EE

.PP
\fBSample 3\fP

.EX
user@host ~ % axilio workflows list -o json
{
  "limit": 20,
  "offset": 0,
  "total": 1,
  "workflows": [
    {
      "workflow": {
        "id": "<workflow-id>",
        "name": "Checkout",
        "platform": "android",
        "status": "active"
      }
    }
  ]
}
.sp
# Exit status: 0
# Notes: Shortened representative JSON output; workflow records may
#        include additional fields and statistics.
.EE


.SH ENVIRONMENT
\fBAXILIO_API_KEY\fP : API credential. Precedence: --api-key,
AXILIO_API_KEY, saved config key, then the saved OAuth session.

.PP
\fBAXILIO_BASE_URL\fP : API host. Precedence: --base-url, AXILIO_BASE_URL,
saved base-url, then https://api.axilio.ai.

.PP
\fBAXILIO_ORG\fP : OAuth organization slug or ID. Precedence: --org,
AXILIO_ORG, saved active organization, then the OAuth session default.
API keys remain scoped to the organization that created them.

.PP
\fBAXILIO_SESSION\fP : Selects a locally saved phone session. Precedence:
--session, AXILIO_SESSION, the only locally saved session, the most
recently started session, then an ambiguity error.

.PP
\fBAXILIO_DASHBOARD_URL\fP : Overrides the dashboard host used for browser
OAuth. It does not change the API host.

.PP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fP : Moves config, OAuth fallback, locally saved
session, and update-check state from $HOME/.config to $XDG_CONFIG_HOME.

.PP
\fBNO_COLOR\fP : Set to 1 to disable ANSI color in help shown on a
terminal; text decoration may remain. When help is redirected,
CLICOLOR_FORCE=1 takes precedence and can restore ANSI color.

.PP
\fBCLICOLOR\fP : Set to 1 to request ANSI color in help when output is a
terminal and TERM is not dumb.

.PP
\fBCLICOLOR_FORCE\fP : Set to 1 to force ANSI color when help is
redirected or TERM=dumb. For redirected help, it takes precedence over
NO_COLOR.

.PP
\fBTERM\fP : TERM=dumb disables ANSI color in help unless CLICOLOR_FORCE=1
is set.


.SH EXIT STATUS
\fB0 (ok)\fP : Success.

.PP
\fB1 (error)\fP : The command failed for a reason that does not fit a more
specific category.

.PP
\fB2 (usage)\fP : Invalid command syntax, argument count, or value; or the
API rejected the request as invalid (HTTP 400 or 422).

.PP
\fB3 (auth)\fP : Missing or invalid credentials, unauthorized access, or
permission denied (HTTP 401 or 403).

.PP
\fB4 (not-found)\fP : A requested resource, phone allocation, or on-screen
element was not found (HTTP 404).

.PP
\fB5 (timeout)\fP : The operation exceeded its timeout or deadline (HTTP
408).

.PP
\fB6 (unavailable)\fP : The Axilio service or phone connection was
unavailable, the phone was offline, the request was rate-limited, or the
server failed (HTTP 429 or 5xx).

.PP
\fB7 (canceled)\fP : The operation was canceled by the user, shell, or
system.


.SH FILES
\fB${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/axilio/config.json\fP : Saved API
key, API host, and active organization. A new file requests mode 0600;
umask may make it more restrictive. Overwriting preserves its mode.

.PP
\fBOS keychain: service axilio-cli, account oauth-tokens\fP : Preferred
storage for browser-OAuth access and refresh tokens.

.PP
\fB${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/axilio/oauth.json\fP : OAuth-token
fallback when the OS keychain is unavailable. A new file requests mode
0600; umask may make it more restrictive. Overwriting preserves its
mode.
.TP
\fB${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/axilio/sessions/<session-id>\&.json\fP
One mode-0600 locally saved session record containing the session ID,
phone ID, type, control URL, and creation time. These local records let
phone commands reconnect; deleting one does not stop the corresponding
Axilio session.

.PP
\fB${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/axilio/current-session\fP : Stores
the ID of the most recently started locally saved session. A new file
requests mode 0600; umask may make it more restrictive. Overwriting
preserves its mode.

.PP
\fB${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/axilio/update-check.json\fP : Daily
release-check cache. Failures reading or writing it do not fail
commands.

.PP
\fB\&./screenshot.png\fP : Default output of \fBaxilio phone screenshot\fR;
--out selects another path and existing contents are overwritten.

.PP
\fB\&.claude/skills/axilio/SKILL.md\fP : Agent instructions written by
\fBaxilio init --agent claude\fR\&.

.PP
\fBAGENTS.md\fP : Shared file updated inside Axilio markers by \fBaxilio
init --agent codex\fR\&.

.PP
\fB\&.cursor/rules/axilio.mdc\fP : Agent instructions written by \fBaxilio
init --agent cursor\fR\&.


.SH NOTES
.SS Resolution precedence
Credentials resolve in this order: --api-key, AXILIO_API_KEY, the saved
config API key, then the saved OAuth session.

.PP
The organization resolves from --org, AXILIO_ORG, the saved active
organization, then the OAuth session default. Note that each API key is
scoped to the organization that created it and cannot switch
organizations with --org.

.PP
API host resolves from --base-url, AXILIO_BASE_URL, saved base-url, then
https://api.axilio.ai.

.PP
Phone command session selection precedence is --session, AXILIO_SESSION,
the only locally saved session, the most recently started session, then
an ambiguity error.

.SS Output behavior
Table output for human readability is the default. Every successful
runnable application command emits valid JSON with -o json; action
commands return a small acknowledgment. Built-in help, completion, and
version output remains text. The sessions start --export command emits
shell text for eval. Notes, prompts, and progress use stderr and are
suppressed in JSON or quiet mode. Quiet and JSON modes do not confirm
destructive actions; pass --yes where offered. API-key, base-URL, and
organization flags affect API-backed commands; they do not select a
local phone session.

.SS Error presentation
Error examples show the message text without terminal formatting. Actual
error output may include an ERROR heading, spacing, and ANSI color.


.SH EXAMPLES
Observe and act on a selected phone session:

.EX
axilio sessions start --phone-type android
axilio phone observe
axilio phone tap --query "the search box"
axilio phone type "coffee shops"
axilio phone observe
.EE

.PP
Start independent sessions in separate shells:

.EX
eval "$(axilio sessions start --export)"
axilio phone screenshot --out screenshot.png
.EE

.PP
Run a workflow and request machine-readable output:

.EX
axilio workflows list -o json
axilio runs start <workflow-id> --count 2 -o json
.EE


